    "result_text": "Done. The build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a two-stage points\u2192level system in `AssignMembershipLevel`, and exposed both fields.\n\n**Points** (start at 0): +2 email present, +1 `namesakeCount == 0`, +2 household of 3+, +3 tenure over 365 days.\n**Level** mapping: 1 (0\u20131 pts), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\nChanges:\n- `AssignMembershipLevel.java` \u2014 rewrote the logic to compute `membershipPoints` and derive `membershipLevel` from it (previously it summed factors directly into a level capped at 3, with level 4 for tenure).\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` field (`membership_points` column) with getter/setter.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `membershipPoints` property (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name) and updated the `membershipLevel` description.\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `membership_points` column so the persisted field round-trips.\n\nThe endpoint pipeline already runs `assignHouseholdSize` and `assignNamesakeCount` before `assignMembershipLevel`, so all inputs are settled when points are computed. The acceptance test (`membershipPoints` = 3, `membershipLevel` = 2 for a fresh owner with email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure) passes.\n\nOne note: `AuditOwnerCreated` still logs only `membershipLevel`, not the new points \u2014 the spec didn't ask for it, so I left the audit line unchanged. Let me know if you'd like it added there too.",
