    "probe_text": "I've read the whole pipeline. Here is the complete, ordered account of `POST /api/owners` (defined by `owners.POST.yml`), step by step. Steps 1\u20139 run outside the transaction; steps 10\u201322 run inside a single `transaction` governance that commits once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition: authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. The whole endpoint is refused unless the caller has role `OWNER_ADMIN`.\n\n## Validations & side-effects, in pipeline order\n\n1. **ValidateOwnerRequiredFields** \u2014 binds the request body (`@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, *no* `@Valid`; this is the only body-binding step, republished as a variable).\n   - *Side-effect:* normalizes `address` in place (`AddressNormalizer`).\n   - *Validation:* rejects with `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (\u2192 errors array) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (after normalization), `city`, `telephone` is null/blank.\n\n2. **ValidateRegistrationDate** \u2014 *validation:* if `registrationDate` is supplied and later than the server's current date, reject with `FutureRegistrationDateException`. (Omitted date \u2192 no check.)\n\n3. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014\n   - *Side-effect:* rewrites `telephone` in place to E.164 form.\n   - *Validation:* if it can't be parsed into a valid number, reject with `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n\n4. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 email is optional (null/blank \u2192 skip).\n   - *Validation:* if present, must match the email regex else `InvalidEmailException` (400).\n   - *Side-effect:* trims and lower-cases `email` in place.\n\n5. **ValidateOwnerEmailDomain** \u2014 optional (null/blank \u2192 skip). *Validation:* if the email's domain is on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), reject with `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n\n6. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 optional (null/blank \u2192 skip). *Validation:* must be exactly 4 digits, and for a city with a known region must fall in that region's range (`PostcodeRegions`); otherwise `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Value left unchanged.\n\n7. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 *validation:* computes a household id from `(normalizedLastName, postcode)`; if it matches any existing owner's household id, reject with `DuplicateOwnerException` (409). Bypassed when `sharesHousehold == true`.\n\n8. **EnsureCityCapacity** \u2014 *validation:* counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed); if \u2265 50, reject with `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n9. **EnsureDailyOwnerLimit** \u2014 *validation:* determines the effective business day (supplied `registrationDate` or server date, weekends rolled forward to Monday); if \u2265 100 owners already have that registration date, reject with `TooManyOwnersTodayException` (429).\n\n*\u2014 transaction begins (governance `transaction` on every step below) \u2014*\n\n10. **BuildOwner** \u2014 *side-effect:* maps the validated DTO into a new `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`).\n\n11. **AssignHousehold** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over normalized last name + postcode.\n\n12. **AssignHouseholdSize** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `householdSize` = count of existing owners sharing that `householdId`, plus 1 (this new owner).\n\n13. **ApplyRegistrationDate** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `registrationDate` to the effective date (supplied, or server date if none), rolled forward off weekends to Monday.\n\n14. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region from postcode + first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256(E.164 telephone + last name).\n\n15. **AssignMembershipNumber** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of registration year).\n\n16. **AssignNamesakeCount** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = number of pre-existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive), snapshot before save.\n\n17. **AssignMembershipLevel** \u2014 *side-effect:* computes `membershipPoints` (+2 email present, +1 no namesakes, +2 household \u2265 3, +3 tenure > 365 days) and sets `membershipLevel` (1/2/3/4 by point bands).\n\n18. **AssignBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if more than 80 existing owners share this owner's registration business day.\n\n19. **AssignPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. Defaults false/null; skipped for a declared household member or when postcode is absent. Otherwise flags true (pointing at the matching owner's id) if an existing owner shares normalized last name + postcode but has a *different* telephone.\n\n20. **SaveOwner** \u2014 *side-effect:* persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n21. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 *side-effect:* emits an `AUDIT` log line with the new id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`.\n\n22. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 *side-effect:* maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. Transaction commits.\n\n### Notes\n- **Validation ordering is deliberate:** required-fields \u2192 date \u2192 telephone/email normalization+format \u2192 email-domain \u2192 postcode \u2192 uniqueness \u2192 city capacity \u2192 daily limit. Because required-fields runs first, a missing field returns 400 before any 404/409/429 concern; normalization happens *before* the checks that depend on the normalized value (e.g. E.164 telephone feeds the customer code and duplicate check; lower-cased email feeds the domain blocklist).\n- Normalizations mutate the bound DTO in place, so persisted and returned values are the normalized forms.\n- `sharesHousehold == true` bypasses both the hard duplicate rejection (step 7) and the soft-duplicate flag (step 19).\n- Any thrown exception is checked and routed to its handler under `officefloor/escalation/`; unmatched ones fall through to Spring `@RestControllerAdvice`.\n\nI read the code without changing anything."
